I've run into something which is probably a feature but I'd like
to think is a bug.  I need some advice.
 
After killing a werejackal or werewolf or were-whatever, I know
enough to avoid eating the were-whatever's corpse, or face the
possibility of becoming a were-whatever.  So, when I kill a were-whatever,
and see that something else is left behind, I figure that it's safe
to eat it, right?  Wrong.  I become a were-whatever.  Arrgh.
 
It seems odd that this would work this way -- but let me give
the dev team the benefit of the doubt here.  I know that when I've
been polymorphed into another creature, I can just let surrounding
animals beat the @#$# out of me until I revert to human form.
When I try this as a were-thing, I become human -- but become
the other thing a short time later.  <sigh>  How do I get rid
of this characteristic?
 
